Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::an_admitted_range_is_inside_the_card_and_the_address`.

The defect: a byte-addressed card gets the block-addressed card's limit, so a block past 4 GB of
bytes is admitted and its byte address wraps in the 32-bit argument: the read or write lands near
the start of the card.

Expected to fail: `assert!((last + 1) * 512 <= 1 << 32)`, on a byte-addressed card larger than 8 Mi
blocks and an lba at or past 8 Mi.

diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs
@@ -356,11 +356,8 @@
     if count == 0 || end > card_blocks {
         return false;
     }
-    if block_addressed {
-        end <= 1 << 32
-    } else {
-        end <= (1 << 32) / BLOCK as u64
-    }
+    let _ = block_addressed;
+    end <= 1 << 32
 }
 
 fn data_command(card: &Card, lba: u64, blocks: u32, write: bool) -> Command {
